  "landing.hero.badge": "AI Integration Platform",
  "landing.hero.title": "Lexiro",
  "landing.hero.slogan": "Complex docs. Simple code.",
  "landing.hero.subslogan": "From documentation to code.",
  "landing.hero.instantly": "Instantly.",
  "landing.hero.description": "AI reads device documentation so developers write integration code, not search queries.",
  "landing.hero.cta": "Get Started",
  "landing.hero.author": "by",

  "landing.elevator.label": "Elevator Pitch",
  "landing.elevator.text": "Lexiro transforms chaotic physical device documentation (PDF, Swagger, web pages) into a <strong>structured knowledge base</strong>, enabling <strong>AI assistants to write working integration code</strong>. We read the docs so you don't have to.",

  "landing.why.title": "Why This Matters",
  "landing.why.text": "Companies integrating physical devices (IP cameras, access control, POS) spend enormous time searching and reading documentation from dozens of manufacturers. Documentation comes in different formats, scattered across websites and PDFs, with no versioning and inaccessible to AI tools. Structured Markdown documentation is what AI assistants (Cursor, Windsurf, GitHub Copilot) need to help with integration.",

  "landing.problems.title": "Problems Today",
  "landing.problems.formatChaos.title": "Format Chaos",
  "landing.problems.formatChaos.text": "PDF, Swagger, web pages, wikis — every vendor has its own format and portal.",
  "landing.problems.noVersioning.title": "No Versioning",
  "landing.problems.noVersioning.text": "Documentation changes with every firmware; unclear which API version is current.",
  "landing.problems.aiCantHelp.title": "AI Can't Help",
  "landing.problems.aiCantHelp.text": "LLMs don't know device APIs; fragments are copy-pasted into chat manually.",
  "landing.problems.codingBlind.title": "Coding Blind",
  "landing.problems.codingBlind.text": "AI in IDE has no access to documentation; code is written with wrong endpoints and parameters.",

  "landing.goals.title": "What We'll Achieve",
  "landing.goals.storage.title": "Unified Documentation Storage",
  "landing.goals.storage.text": "All documentation in one place, in Markdown, versioned by firmware. Conversion from PDF (with OCR), Swagger/OpenAPI, and web pages.",
  "landing.goals.audit.title": "Full Audit & Control",
  "landing.goals.audit.text": "Every import is a job with history: who, when, result, duration. Diff between versions shows API changes.",
  "landing.goals.aiCode.title": "AI Writes Integration Code",
  "landing.goals.aiCode.text": "In AI IDE, ask \"how to connect Hikvision via ISAPI\" and get working code with real endpoints and parameters.",
  "landing.goals.aiChat.title": "AI Chat with Documentation",
  "landing.goals.aiChat.text": "Built-in chat: question → answer with citations from documents. Choose context: all devices, vendor, or firmware.",
  "landing.goals.multilingual.title": "Multilingual + Translation",
  "landing.goals.multilingual.text": "Any documentation language; optional translation to English before conversion (LLM, DeepL, Google Translate).",
  "landing.goals.speedup.title": "3–5× Development Speedup",
  "landing.goals.speedup.text": "Instead of hours reading PDFs — semantic search across the knowledge base and integration code generation.",

  "landing.howItWorks.title": "How It Works",
  "landing.howItWorks.subtitle": "Click each step to see usage scenario details.",
  "landing.howItWorks.step": "Step",
  "landing.howItWorks.step1.title": "Upload Documentation",
  "landing.howItWorks.step1.text": "User uploads PDF manual for Hikvision DS-2CD2143G2-I camera (firmware 5.7.21) via Import Wizard. Document language doesn't matter — the system detects the format, user specifies OCR language. Optional English translation. Chinese, Korean, Japanese — any language.",
  "landing.howItWorks.step1.code": "POST /api/jobs\n{ \"source_type\": \"pdf\", \"device\": \"DS-2CD2143G2-I\",\n  \"firmware\": \"5.7.21\", \"ocr\": true, \"translate\": false }",
  "landing.howItWorks.step2.title": "Automatic Conversion",
  "landing.howItWorks.step2.text": "Background job starts conversion: OCR recognizes text from PDF, parses tables and document structure, converts to clean Markdown with headings, code blocks, and tables.",
  "landing.howItWorks.step2.code": "Job #47 [RUNNING] ████████░░ 78%\n→ OCR: 142 pages processed\n→ Tables extracted: 23\n→ Code blocks found: 67\n→ Estimated: 2 min remaining",
  "landing.howItWorks.step3.title": "Versioned Storage",
  "landing.howItWorks.step3.text": "Result is saved to S3 with firmware versioning. If a document for this device already existed — a new version is created, diff shows API changes.",
  "landing.howItWorks.step3.code": "S3: lexiro/devices/ds-2cd2143g2-i/5.7.21/\n  └── isapi-reference/\n      ├── v1.md  (2024-01-15, 234KB)\n      └── v2.md  (2024-06-20, 251KB)  ← NEW\n\nDiff: +17 endpoints, ~3 changed, -2 deprecated",
  "landing.howItWorks.step4.title": "AI Indexing",
  "landing.howItWorks.step4.text": "Chunking pipeline splits Markdown into semantic fragments by headings (H1/H2/H3). Each fragment is vectorized via embedding API and stored in pgvector for semantic search.",
  "landing.howItWorks.step4.code": "Chunking: 251KB → 187 chunks\nEmbedding: 187 chunks → 187 vectors (1536 dims)\nIndex: HNSW cosine similarity\n\nChunk example:\n  heading: \"ISAPI > Cameras > GET /channels\"\n  tokens: 847",
  "landing.howItWorks.step5.title": "AI Writes Working Code",
  "landing.howItWorks.step5.text": "Developer in AI IDE asks: \"How to get camera list via ISAPI?\" MCP server finds relevant chunks, LLM generates working code with correct endpoints and parameters.",
  "landing.howItWorks.step5.code": "// AI IDE → MCP Server → RAG → LLM\n\nimport requests\n\ndef get_channels(host, user, pwd):\n    url = f\"http://{host}/ISAPI/System/Video/inputs/channels\"\n    from requests.auth import HTTPDigestAuth\n    r = requests.get(url, auth=HTTPDigestAuth(user, pwd), verify=False)\n    return r.json()[\"VideoInputChannelList\"]\n\n# ✓ Endpoint verified from firmware 5.7.21 docs\n# ✓ Auth method: HTTP Digest (from ISAPI spec)",

  "landing.footer.copyright": "© 2026 Lexiro",
  "landing.footer.by": "by",
  "landing.footer.author": "Aleh Vaitsekhovich",

